course: dictionary
lesson: 2562
title: Handling words with care
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Delicately is an adverb. It tells you how something is done. Read the words around it for clues. «An elephant's trunk can hold things as delicately as fingers.» Fingers are careful when they pick things up, so delicately must mean gently and carefully, so nothing gets broken or hurt.
explain: Try the swap test. Put your meaning into the sentence in place of the hard word. «She held the eggshell gently and carefully» still makes sense, so your meaning is right. If your meaning made the sentence silly, you would need to think again.
explain: The same word can change its feel depending on what it describes. «Delicately painted flowers» means painted in a fine, light, graceful way. «Delicately spiced» food has a light, gentle flavour. «Put it delicately» means choose your words with care so you do not upset anyone.
fact: Delicately is an adverb: it tells you how something is done.
fact: The comparative form is more delicately.
fact: Delicately means gently and carefully, so as not to break or hurt something.
fact: It can also mean in a fine, light and graceful way, or with a light, gentle flavour in food.
fact: Used with people's feelings, delicately means tactfully, with care not to upset anyone.
exercise: «She held the eggshell delicately so it did not crack.» How did she hold it? | Roughly and fast | *Gently and carefully | Upside down on purpose | Loudly
exercise: «The artist drew delicately painted flowers.» What does delicately mean here? | Thickly and roughly | Very quickly | Loudly | *In a fine, light and graceful way
exercise: Mum says, «He asked about her illness delicately.» What does delicately mean? | Rudely, to get an answer fast | *Tactfully, with care not to upset her | Loudly, so everyone could hear | Quickly, without thinking
test: «The soup was delicately spiced.» What does delicately mean here? | Full of salt | Very hot and burning | Cold | *With a light, gentle flavour
test: «Scientists handle insects delicately.» How do they handle them? | Roughly | Angrily | *Gently, so as not to hurt them | Too fast to see
exam: Which phrase means the same as delicately in «hold things delicately»? | Very loudly | Roughly and quickly | Without looking at them | *Gently and carefully
